<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Evelthon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Euelthon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Evelthon was king of Salamis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> in the 6th century BCE. He is credited with some of the island's earliest coins and, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, dedicated a censer at Delphi and refused <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pheretime">Pheretime</a> of Cyrene an army, giving her instead a golden spindle and distaff. His descendants ruled Salamis into the 5th century BCE.</p></div>
